{
 "summary": "Enables the `-Wunused` compiler warning flag and related flags in the build system. Across 159 files, it fixes existing warnings primarily by removing unused function parameter names, commenting them out, or annotating them with `[[maybe_unused]]`.",
 "problem": "The build does not enforce `-Wunused`, allowing dead code, unused parameters, and unused variables to accumulate in the codebase undetected. In some cases, unused variables or functions reveal logic that was accidentally omitted rather than deliberately dead code.",
 "evidence": [
  "The author notes numerous recent dead code removals and highlights #36137: 'as an instance of what was thought to be dead code, but it'd actually just been forgotten to be used: #36137. It could be beneficial to get `-Wunused` & related flags enabled, to catch dead/unused code in CI.'",
  "The author notes compiler warnings that also help enforce idioms like `inline constexpr` headers: 'Enabling some of these flags may also help enforce other stuff, like `inline constexpr` usage (#35852).'"
 ],
 "dependencies": {
  "depends_on": [],
  "enables": [
   "#36275"
  ]
 },
 "scope_notes": "Contains three `[[nomerge]]` commits modifying subtree code (LevelDB, Minisketch, libmultiprocess) that require upstream PRs before this can be merged into Bitcoin Core. The remaining diff is a large, mechanical refactoring touching over 150 files to silence compiler parameter warnings.",
 "changed_since_previous": "Rebased and pruned slightly from 168 to 159 files; related pull request #36275 (enabling `-Wunused-const-variable`) was merged in the interim.",
 "card": "This draft RFC enables `-Wunused` and related compiler warning flags in the CMake build configuration. Without `-Wunused` enforced in CI, unused variables and parameters accumulate unnoticed, occasionally hiding bugs where intended logic was omitted (such as #36137). The pull request resolves existing warnings across nearly 160 files by omitting or annotating unused parameter names. Merging requires upstream subtree updates to LevelDB, Minisketch, and libmultiprocess.",
